# Mock Data Phase

## Do
- Drive UI with in-memory / hardcoded mock models.
- Fake repositories or static sample lists are fine.
- UI may show prices, ratings, and product info from mocks.

## Do not
- Add real network clients, API base URLs, or remote auth.
- Build Cart, Checkout, Payment, or Place-order flows/screens.
- Block UI work waiting for a backend.

## Product detail note
- Do **not** show Add to cart / Buy now (or other purchase CTAs) on PDP.
- Quantity / Save may exist as **visual placeholders** only — no cart wiring.
- Do not wire a real checkout path.

## When to use
- Always, until the project explicitly moves to the API phase.

## When to update
- API integration starts → replace or rewrite this rule as an `api-phase` rule.
- Purchase flow is added back → update out-of-scope list and `screens.md`.
